---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo';

// Keep this date in step with any change to the text below.
const lastUpdated = '30 July 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | AH Design"
  description="How AH Design collects, uses and protects personal data submitted through this website, who we share it with, and the rights you have under the GDPR."
  schema={[
    breadcrumbSchema([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy' },
    ]),
  ]}
  htmlClass="no-js vlt-is--careers-single vlt-is--header-fullscreen vlt-is--footer-style-1 vlt-is--footer-fixed"
>
  <div class="vlt-site-overlay"></div>
  <main class="vlt-main">
    <div class="vlt-page-content">
      <div class="vlt-page-title vlt-page-title--style-4">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-7 offset-md-1">
              <h1 class="vlt-page-title__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-3">
              <div
                class="vlt-page-title__phantom-title lax"
                data-lax-translate-x="0 0, vw (vw*0.5)"
                data-lax-opacity="1 1, 250 0"
                data-lax-anchor=".vlt-page-title"
              >
                Privacy
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="content"></div>

      <section>
        <div class="vlt-gap-100"></div>
        <div class="container">
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-10 offset-md-1">
              <p class="fz-3 text-justify">
                This policy explains what personal data AH Design (&ldquo;we&rdquo;) collects
                through <a href="/">ahdesign.website</a>, why we collect it, who we share it with,
                and what you can ask us to do with it. We are the data controller for that data.
              </p>
              <p class="fz-3 text-justify">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

              <div class="vlt-gap-60"></div>
              <h2>What we collect</h2>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                We collect personal data in only one place on this site: the contact form and the
                order form. When you submit one of them, we receive the details you typed into it.
              </p>
              <ul class="vlt-styled-list vlt-styled-list--style-3">
                <li>Your name</li>
                <li>Your email address</li>
                <li>Your phone number, if you provide one</li>
                <li>Your company name, if you provide one</li>
                <li>The subject or the package you selected</li>
                <li>The message you write</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                We do not run advertising or analytics trackers on this site, and we do not build
                profiles of visitors. We do not knowingly collect data from children. We never ask
                for payment card details through this website.
              </p>

              <div class="vlt-gap-60"></div>
              <h2>Why we use it, and on what legal basis</h2>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                We use what you send us to reply to your enquiry, to prepare a quote, and to carry
                out any work you go on to order. Under the GDPR our legal basis is Article 6(1)(b),
                steps taken at your request before entering into a contract, and Article 6(1)(f),
                our legitimate interest in answering people who contact us and in keeping the forms
                free of spam and abuse.
              </p>

              <div class="vlt-gap-60"></div>
              <h2>Spam protection and server logs</h2>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                The forms are protected by Cloudflare Turnstile. To tell a person from a bot,
                Turnstile receives your IP address and basic information about your browser, and it
                stores a short-lived cookie in your browser for that check. This is strictly
                necessary to keep the forms usable, so it does not rely on your consent. Our host,
                Cloudflare, also keeps standard security and traffic logs that include IP addresses.
              </p>

              <div class="vlt-gap-60"></div>
              <h2>Cookies</h2>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                This site sets only the strictly necessary cookies described above, placed by
                Cloudflare for security and spam protection. There are no analytics, advertising or
                profiling cookies, which is why you are not asked to accept a cookie banner. If we
                add analytics or advertising tools in future, we will update this policy and ask for
                your consent first where the law requires it.
              </p>

              <div class="vlt-gap-60"></div>
              <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                We do not sell your personal data and we do not share it for anyone else's
                marketing. We do rely on a small number of service providers to run the site and
                deliver your message to us:
              </p>
              <ul class="vlt-styled-list vlt-styled-list--style-3">
                <li>
                  Cloudflare, Inc. hosts this website and provides the Turnstile spam protection.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Google (Gmail) delivers each form submission to our inbox, where it is stored.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Telegram Messenger sends us an instant notification containing the contents of
                  your submission, so we see new enquiries quickly.
                </li>
              </ul>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                These providers process data on servers that may sit outside the European Economic
                Area, including in the United States. Such transfers are covered by the European
                Commission's standard contractual clauses or by an adequacy decision, depending on
                the provider. We may also disclose data where the law requires it.
              </p>

              <div class="vlt-gap-60"></div>
              <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                Enquiries that do not lead to work are kept for up to two years, so that we have
                context if you come back to us. Where you become a client, we keep project
                correspondence for as long as we work together and then for the period our
                accounting and tax obligations require. You can ask us to delete your data sooner.
              </p>

              <div class="vlt-gap-60"></div>
              <h2>Your rights</h2>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                Under the GDPR you can ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold about you, ask
                us to correct it, ask us to delete it, ask us to restrict how we use it, object to
                our use of it where we rely on legitimate interests, and ask us to send it to you or
                another provider in a portable format.
              </p>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will respond within one
                month. If you think we have handled your data badly, you can complain to the Bulgarian
                Commission for Personal Data Protection at <a
                  href="https://www.cpdp.bg"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener">cpdp.bg</a
                >, or to the supervisory authority where you live.
              </p>

              <div class="vlt-gap-60"></div>
              <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                If we change how we handle personal data, we will update this page and change the
                date at the top. Material changes will be highlighted here.
              </p>

              <div class="vlt-gap-60"></div>
              <h2>Contact us</h2>
              <div class="vlt-gap-30"></div>
              <p class="text-justify">
                AH Design<br />
                Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a><br />
                Phone: <a href={`tel:${SITE.phone}`}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="vlt-gap-120"></div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
